\subsection{Phase E: hybrid recovery and bounded non-OU mismatch in the funnel metric}
\label{sec:stability-widening-phase-e}

The hybrid and model-mismatch results use the same source-node Lyapunov metric
$W_i$ as the normal-Live and handoff certificates.  No separate Euclidean or
Phase-B quantitative metric is introduced.

\subsubsection{Tilt relock as a reset-to-funnel map}

Let a tilt relock satisfy
\begin{equation}
 -\vct f_T^B=g\vct d+\vct a_T,
 \qquad \|\vct a_T\|\le\bar f_T<g,
 \qquad
 \bar\theta_T:=\sin^{-1}(\bar f_T/g).
 \label{eq:widen-tilt-reset-force}
\end{equation}
The same tangent-ball argument as Lemma~\ref{lem:widen-global-reset} gives
\begin{equation}
 \theta_\perp^+\le\bar\theta_T
 \label{eq:widen-tilt-reset-bound}
\end{equation}
independently of the pre-reset tilt.  The preserve-yaw source reset leaves the
adopted heading gauge unchanged and does not hard-reset the additive navigation
coordinates.

Let $i^-$ and $i^+$ be the pre/post reset source nodes and let
$W_{U,i^-}$ denote the part of the pre-reset metric associated with coordinates
that remain physically continuous across the jump.  Rigorous enclosure of the
exact reset, covariance reseed, and destination metric gives finite
$\kappa_U$ and $\delta_T^{\rm an}$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 W_{i^+}^+\le\kappa_U W_{U,i^-}^-+\delta_T^{\rm an},
 \qquad
 \delta_T^{\rm an}:=
 c_T(1-\cos\bar\theta_T)+c_{T,d}\bar d_T^2.}
 \label{eq:widen-reset-to-set}
\end{equation}
The discarded pre-reset tilt energy does not appear in the multiplicative term.

During the mandatory cooldown, tile the source execution by the certified word
family and define the worst reachable cooldown contraction
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \lambda_{\rm cool}^{\rm an}:=
 \sup_{\text{reachable cooldown tilings}}
 \prod_{w\in\mathrm{tiling}}\lambda_w<1.}
 \label{eq:widen-cooldown-factor}
\end{equation}
Let $\gamma_{\rm cool}$ be the rigorously accumulated bounded-input contribution
through the same word sequence.  Then
\begin{equation}
 W_{j+1}^-
 \le\lambda_{\rm cool}^{\rm an}W_j^+
 +\gamma_{\rm cool}.
 \label{eq:widen-cooldown-flow}
\end{equation}

\begin{theorem}[Recurrent tilt-reset funnel small gain]
\label{thm:widen-hybrid-small-gain}
Suppose every reset and cooldown prefix remains inside its certified source-node
geodesic/funnel domain and
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mu_T^{\rm an}:=\kappa_U\lambda_{\rm cool}^{\rm an}<1.}
 \label{eq:widen-hybrid-mu}
\end{equation}
Then successive pre-reset sections satisfy
\begin{equation}
 W_{j+1}^-
 \le\mu_T^{\rm an}W_j^-
 +\lambda_{\rm cool}^{\rm an}\delta_T^{\rm an}
 +\gamma_{\rm cool},
 \label{eq:widen-reset-poincare}
\end{equation}
and therefore
\begin{equation}
 \limsup_{j\to\infty}W_j^-
 \le
 \frac{\lambda_{\rm cool}^{\rm an}\delta_T^{\rm an}
       +\gamma_{\rm cool}}
      {1-\mu_T^{\rm an}}.
 \label{eq:widen-reset-ultimate}
\end{equation}
The pre-reset tilt magnitude does not appear in the multiplicative loop gain.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Apply Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-reset-to-set}, use
$W_{U,i^-}^-\le W_{i^-}^-$, then apply the certified cooldown word product and
iterate the resulting scalar affine recursion.  The source cooldown excludes
Zeno behavior.
\end{proof}

Magnetic hard re-gauging is a bounded symmetry change of the adopted horizontal
coordinate frame.  Its exact jump is certified between source-node funnels; on
the gravity-only quotient it is the identity equivalence class.  It does not
require an artificial attitude-capture radius.

\subsubsection{Bounded departures from the OU latent-acceleration model}

The OU state is a regularizer rather than a claim that physical ocean
acceleration is an exact OU sample path.  Write
\begin{equation}
 \dot{\vct a}_w
 =-\tau_m^{-1}\vct a_w+\vct w_{OU}+\vct d_m,
 \label{eq:widen-model-mismatch}
\end{equation}
where $\vct d_m$ collects bounded non-OU dynamics, unresolved harmonics,
hydrodynamic forcing, and correlation-model mismatch.

For every certified source word $w:i\to j$, compactness of the exact lifted map
and the strict zero-input word margin imply a finite disturbance gain
$c_{d,w}$ such that, for the declared input budget,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 W_j(\mathcal F_w(e,d))
 \le\lambda_w W_i(e)+c_{d,w}\|d\|_{\infty,w}^2,
 \qquad \lambda_w<1.}
 \label{eq:widen-deterministic-drift}
\end{equation}
This is the deterministic funnel inequality used throughout the deployed
certificate; all non-OU forcing enters through the same exact source word map.
Define
\begin{equation}
 \lambda_d:=\max_w\lambda_w<1,
 \qquad
 c_d:=\max_w c_{d,w}<\infty.
 \label{eq:widen-deterministic-gains}
\end{equation}

\begin{theorem}[Practical ISS under bounded non-OU forcing]
\label{thm:widen-model-mismatch-iss}
If the declared funnel is robustly invariant under the total bounded-input
budget, then at certified word boundaries
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 W_n\le\lambda_d^{\,n-j}W_j
 +\frac{c_d}{1-\lambda_d}
  \|\vct d\|_{\infty,[j,n)}^2.}
 \label{eq:widen-model-iss}
\end{equation}
Thus bounded $\vct d_m$ changes the ultimate bound but does not destroy
practical stability.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Equation~\eqref{eq:widen-deterministic-drift} holds on every source-complete
word.  Taking the uniform word constants and iterating the scalar recursion
gives Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-model-iss}; certified prefix bounds control all
physical samples between word boundaries.
\end{proof}

A correlation-time mismatch enters explicitly.  If a physical reference model
uses $\tau_*$ while the filter uses $\tau_m$, then
\begin{equation}
 -\tau_*^{-1}\vct a_w
 =-\tau_m^{-1}\vct a_w
 +\underbrace{(\tau_m^{-1}-\tau_*^{-1})\vct a_w}_{\vct d_\tau}.
 \label{eq:widen-tau-mismatch}
\end{equation}
For $\|\vct a_w\|\le A_w$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \|\vct d_\tau\|
 \le |\tau_m^{-1}-\tau_*^{-1}|A_w.}
 \label{eq:widen-tau-mismatch-bound}
\end{equation}
Hence the same funnel ISS gain quantifies bounded correlation-time error.

\begin{remark}[Interpretation of the OU assumption]
\label{rem:widen-ou-regularizer}
OU dynamics define the nominal regularizing state transition; bounded departures
are source-word disturbances with explicit gain.  Wave-spectrum and reduced-MSE
arguments used to choose $\tau$ and $\sigma_{aw}$ remain performance arguments,
not prerequisites for deterministic stability.
\end{remark}
